<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
  <section xml:id="two-d-games-space-farm-09-finishing-up">
    <title>Finishing Up</title>
    <introduction>
    <p>
        The main thing that the game is still missing is a background. To add a background, 
        open the main scene and add add a TextureRect. Move the texture rect to be the first child of Main, so that it is behind
        Player and all of the other nodes. In the inspector load the art/hubble-background1152.png file for the Texture.
    </p>
    </introduction>
    <subsection xml:id="two-d-games-space-farm-finising-up-p1">
      <title>Final Playtesting Modifications</title>
      <p>
        Run the main scene. Check to see if the player is visible enough. If not, try one of the other Ship files for the Player's Sprite2D. In addiiton, 
        you could find a different ship for the player if you'd like. (Just make sure to change the collision polygon 2d's shape.)
      </p>
      <p>
        While playing the game, experiment with different timing for how often plants spawn, how fast the ship thrusts and turns, and how far/big the 
        collector should get.
      </p>
      </subsection>
      <subsection xml:id="two-d-games-space-farm-finising-up-p2">
      <title>Part 2</title>
      <p>
      </p>
      </subsection>
      
    </section>
